{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>And if he comes, he shall come.</b> At the end of the second week." "<b>And he shall see, and behold the plague has not spread.</b> This verse comes to teach about one that stands unchanged in the first week and in the second — what is done to it? You might say he declares it clean, as the verse implies: 'and the priest shall cleanse the house' — Scripture says, 'for the plague is healed' — I declared clean only that which is healed; and 'healed' means only a house that was quarantined and plastered and the plague did not return — but this one requires removal, scraping, plastering, and a third week; and so the verse is expounded: 'And if he comes, he shall come in the second, and he shall see and behold it has not spread' — he shall plaster it — and there is no plastering without removal and scraping — and 'after the house is plastered, the priest shall cleanse the house' — if it did not return at the end of the week, 'for the plague is healed'; and if it returned, it has already been stated regarding one that returns that it requires demolition.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:32.168049188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}